{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--personal-deity-on-shoulder","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers"],"statement":{"en":"In traditional Ainu belief, a deity rests on each individual's shoulder and determines their personality and destiny.","ja":"伝統的なアイヌの信仰では、各個人の肩に神が憑いており、その人の性格や運命を決定づけるとされている。"},"type":"other","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"epistemic","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0259-05","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--nispa-honorific-title-sakhalin","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--honorific-fourth-person"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, nispa functions as an honorific title attached to the names of distinguished men.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語において、nispaは有力な男性の名につけて呼ぶ敬称として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"factual","conditions":[]},"forms":["nispa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0068-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--honorific-geographic-distribution","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--honorific-fourth-person"],"statement":{"en":"Honorific expressions are reported to be rare in classical yukar and northern and eastern dialects, appearing consistently only in Hidaka and Iburi through prolonged contact with Japanese.","ja":"アイヌ語の敬語表現は古典的ユーカラや北部・東部方言では稀であり、和人との長期的接触があった日高・胆振方言においてのみ一貫して見られるとされる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"epistemic","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0032-08","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--nominalized-honorific-expressions","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--honorific-fourth-person"],"statement":{"en":"Nominalized expressions are sometimes employed as honorific expressions even in everyday speech.","ja":"日常語においても、名詞化された表現が尊敬表現として用いられることがある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"factual","conditions":[]},"forms":["kur"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0329-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--fire-deity-prayer-title","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--prayer-register"],"statement":{"en":"In southwestern Hokkaido prayer register, the fire deity is addressed with the genre-specific honorific title mosir kor huci.","ja":"北海道南西部方言の祈り詞において、火の神は祈り詞というジャンルに特有の尊称 mosir kor huci で呼びかけられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"factual","conditions":["prayer register"]},"forms":["mosir kor huci"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:endo2022@handbook-epub/l0064-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--sakhalin-prayer-lexical-stratum","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--prayer-register"],"statement":{"en":"In the Sakhalin Ainu ceremonial prayer register, a distinct lexical stratum is preserved, such as using ape for 'fire' rather than the everyday unci.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語の儀礼祈祷レジスターでは特殊な語彙層が保たれており、日常語の unci に代えて ape「火」が用いられる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"factual","conditions":["prayer register"]},"forms":["ape","unci"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:tangiku2022@handbook-epub/l0056-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--sakhalin-taboo-hunting-vocabulary","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--taboo-vocabulary"],"statement":{"en":"Sakhalin Ainu possessed a vocabulary of about one hundred conventional taboo words used during hunting, sea voyages, and for conversational secrecy.","ja":"樺太アイヌ語には、狩猟や航海中、あるいは第三者からの秘匿のために用いられる約100語の忌み言葉・隠語が存在した。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"factual","conditions":["hunting","sea voyages","secrecy"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:majewicz2022@handbook-epub/l0024-05","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--mountain-and-sea-taboo-vocabulary","differs_in":"scope","note":"Sakhalin-specific inventory of hunting and voyage taboo vocabulary."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--mountain-and-sea-taboo-vocabulary","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--taboo-vocabulary"],"statement":{"en":"Taboo words requiring lexical substitution when entering the mountains or going out to sea exist in Ainu.","ja":"アイヌ語には、山に入った時や海に出た時に語彙置換を行わなければならない忌詞が存在する。"},"type":"existence","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"factual","conditions":["mountains","sea"]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0519-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--tokachi-mountain-taboo-words","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--taboo-vocabulary"],"statement":{"en":"In the Tokachi dialect, mountain taboo words replace ordinary village words with words of different meaning to avoid alerting mountain deities to marine things.","ja":"十勝方言の山言葉では、山の神に海のものを悟らせないよう、日常の里言葉を別の意味の語で置き換える。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/tokachi"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"factual","conditions":["in the mountains"]},"forms":["sippo","huna","sas","situkap","atuy","to","cip","kitci","herekus","ciray","sake","wakka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0525-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--mountain-and-sea-taboo-vocabulary","differs_in":"scope","note":"Tokachi-specific mountain taboo avoidance vocabulary."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--shari-offshore-taboo-words","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--taboo-vocabulary"],"statement":{"en":"In the Shari dialect, offshore taboo words substitute special terms for ordinary village words during sea mammal hunting.","ja":"斜里方言の沖言葉では、海獣猟などの際に通常の里言葉に対して特殊な語彙置換が行われる。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/northeast/kitami"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"factual","conditions":["offshore hunting"]},"forms":["tukar","ciramantep","konru","sotki","cip","nimam","cippake","repunney","cipsupuy","peunta","wakkakep","cirirkay"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0525-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--mountain-and-sea-taboo-vocabulary","differs_in":"scope","note":"Shari-specific offshore sea-mammal hunting taboo vocabulary."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--shiraoi-offshore-taboo-words","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--taboo-vocabulary"],"statement":{"en":"In the Shiraoi dialect, offshore taboo language replaces ordinary village words with specific avoidance terms.","ja":"白老方言の沖言葉では、通常の里言葉が特定の忌避語に置き換えられる。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/horobetsu"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"factual","conditions":["offshore"]},"forms":["isepo","tukisarus","same","herasnucep","ikema","penup","humpe","pisotki","meko","cape"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0526-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--mountain-and-sea-taboo-vocabulary","differs_in":"scope","note":"Shiraoi-specific offshore taboo vocabulary."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--eastern-hidaka-rabbit-taboo-word","revision":1,"topic":"topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topics":["topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--taboo-vocabulary"],"statement":{"en":"In eastern Hidaka offshore hunting taboo speech, 'rabbit' was referred to as kaykuma rather than isepo to avoid association with rough sea whitecaps.","ja":"日高東部の沖狩忌詞において、白波（isepo tereke）を連想させる isepo を避けるため、ウサギは kaykuma と言い換えられた。"},"type":"variation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"some","modality":"epistemic","conditions":["offshore hunting"]},"forms":["isepo","kaykuma","isepo tereke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0526-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[{"kind":"refines","claim":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--mountain-and-sea-taboo-vocabulary","differs_in":"scope","note":"Eastern Hidaka offshore taboo avoidance term for rabbit."},{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers--shiraoi-offshore-taboo-words","differs_in":"dialect","note":"Eastern Hidaka substitutes kaykuma for rabbit, whereas Shiraoi substitutes tukisarus."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
